  "supportingPhenomena": "• Stomach acid helps digest food, but too much acid causes heartburn, which an antacid relieves.\n• Wood ash water feels soapy and can be used for washing, while lemon juice tastes sour and can remove stains.\n• Bleach changes the colour of stained clothes in laundry, and the label warns against mixing it with other cleaners.\n• Farmers in the Rift Valley and Kericho add lime or fertilisers to soil, and runoff from fertilisers can make Lake Victoria green with algae (eutrophication).\n• Salt is spread on roads in some countries in winter, and food companies use salt to preserve fish and meat.",
