        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'You are researchers. Record the salt's name, what it does, and your source. Handle devices carefully and use only approved sites or the cards.' Circulate and ask: 'Which salt is this? Is it the same salt as in Mama Amina's tin?' Wait 10 seconds for answers. Point out where facts must match the cards: fertilisers (ammonium nitrate, calcium ammonium nitrate, gypsum/lime); fish and meat preservation; oral rehydration salts, Epsom salt, antacids; washing soda softening water; calcium chloride settling dust on murram roads, noting that salt to melt ice is not needed in Kenya. Ask: 'Does your source say who wrote it? Do two sources agree?' At sharing time cold-call 5 learners, one per area, to report one fact to the whole class.",
