        "teacherMoves": "Set the rules: 'One speaker at a time, respect every opinion, and back each claim with evidence.' Give 2 minutes of preparation. Ask: 'Farmer Kiprop wants better tea yields. What would you advise him about how much fertiliser to use?' Wait 15 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners from each side for one claim plus evidence. Prompt: 'How does run-off reach Lake Victoria, and what happens to the fish?' Wait 10 seconds and ask learners to connect oxygen depletion to fish death. Then ask: 'Is salt itself the problem, or is it the amount and where it goes?' Cold-call 3 learners. Finish by having learners write one sentence beginning 'Salts are useful when...'.",
